{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwYTrv1yMypjSL6xTV9k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I didn't open the dashboard or wait for the rule to run, so neither has been tested. The rule's status is still \"pending\" because it hasn't run yet.\n\n**Data:** The logs data view uses `timestamp` as its time field. Its main fields are:\n- `response` (the status code, stored as a string)\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `clientip`\n- `machine.os`\n- `request` and `url`\n- `referer`\n- `agent`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-5da01f6f Web logs overview\" has 5 panels over the last 7 days:\n- total requests\n- requests over time\n- responses by status code\n- bytes by file extension\n- top source countries\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-5da01f6f 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute. It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` where `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]`, over a 5-minute window. It fires when that count is above 10.\n\nThe rule has no action attached, so it will only show up as an alert in Kibana and won't send a notification anywhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1350,"cache_read_input_tokens":19083,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1350},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"cf1c4985-f80d-4ce6-87ef-442a02413ce3","timestamp":"2026-10-12T02:20:08.318Z","request_id":"req_011CfwYTrh8BgLE2M1RfhedV"}
